pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: the WCNF parser took a literal's variable identity from its
% spelling (`"x" + lex.slice()`), not its value, so `1`, `01`, `001` and `+1`
% interned four different variables. The hard clause `x1` and the soft clause
% `~x1` were read as constraints on unrelated variables, silently relaxing the
% formula: the solution `x1 ~x01` was accepted and `BOUNDS 0 0` verified, while
% the real instance forces x1 and pays the soft clause's weight of 1.
f 1;
sol x1 ~x01;
output NONE;
conclusion BOUNDS 0 0;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
